Run typed eval/call/workspace requests. Validate call arguments, retain successful results under unique workspace handles, and optionally append request/result/error/timestamp to an InteractionLog. Retain referenced objects. Bind/release handles through validated names. Internal workspace evaluation preserves user it and shell binding.

kind promise validates a normal typed call, creates and starts a Promise in the workspace, and retains its returned identity.

kind example executes the example object, decodes its WorkspaceResult and retains the typed outcome.

Before executing a standard control action, capture its semantic replay request. Execute the original control, but record and expose the captured receiver/message for replay and examples. Retain original and normalized object references. A binding-capture failure is returned separately and prevents misleading recording output without suppressing execution.

Optional participantId selects and validates the participant scratch workspace. Retain results and handles in that workspace, return participantId/workspaceId and append attributed interaction activity. Object-specific scratch workspaces are keyed beneath the participant workspace. Result bind/release targets its supplied participant. Omitted identity keeps legacy behavior.
